+# Local Stack Troubleshooting
+
+Logs are under `/Users/kantaro/Downloads/toc/.codex/run/toc-server/` (`backend.log`, `frontend.log`). Inspect the failed component's recent log first.
+
+The backend is `server.app:app`; the frontend is `server/web`. The host backend uses the host-reachable Postgres URL, defaulting to `postgresql://toc:toc@127.0.0.1:5432/toc`. The local helper sets `TOC_SERVER_AUTH_DISABLED=1`; do not extend that to a remotely exposed server.
+
+Use existing helper overrides only when needed:
+
+- `TOC_LOCAL_REPO_ROOT`: explicitly selected repository/output root.
+- `TOC_DATABASE_URL`: host-reachable database connection.
+- `TOC_CODEX_BIN`: Codex executable; normal local preference is `/opt/homebrew/bin/codex`.
+- `TOC_CODEX_HOME`: stable Codex auth/config home for launch and checks.
+- `TOC_FRONTEND_NODE_DIR` or `TOC_NPM`: frontend runtime override.
+- `TOC_SKIP_DB_START=1`: explicitly requested skip of DB startup.
+
+The helper also probes Codex app-server initialization, thread creation, and a short no-op turn. HTTP health alone does not prove the generation transport works. Reuse that result, and distinguish a transport failure from a content or run-validation failure. Diagnose a failed check before retrying rather than repeatedly restarting unchanged processes.
